+# Synthetic Playwright Identities — Contract
+
+## Overview
+
+Idempotent provisioning contract for three synthetic Audiobookshelf identities
+used by Playwright E2E tests. The provisioning script creates/manages Keycloak
+users, rotates passwords, and reconciles group membership.
+
+## Identities
+
+| Username | Role | Group | Purpose |
+|----------|------|-------|---------|
+| `pw-e2e-abs-user` | E2E user | `audiobookshelf-users` | Standard user flows |
+| `pw-e2e-abs-admin` | E2E admin | `audiobookshelf-admins` | Admin role coverage |
+| `pw-e2e-abs-denied` | E2E denied | (none) | Authorization negative tests |
+
+## Naming Convention
+
+- Username: `pw-e2e-<service>-<role>` (PWR-020 compliant)
+- Display name: same as username (visible automation marker)
+- Email: `pw-e2e-<service>-<role>@homelab.test` (no real data)
+- No personal data (PWR-021 compliant)
+
+## Provisioning Script
+
+**Path:** `pi/audiobookshelf/scripts/setup-playwright-identities.sh`
+
+### Modes
+
+| Mode | Flag | Behavior |
+|------|------|----------|
+| Dry-run | `--dry-run` (default) | Read-only checks: verify realm, groups, client exist via kcadm |
+| Commit | `--commit` | Full provisioning: create users, rotate passwords, reconcile groups |
+
+### Commit Mode Behavior
+
+1. Assert realm, groups, client exist (fail-closed)
+2. For each identity:
+   - Create user if not exists
+   - Rotate password (new random 24-char password per run)
+   - Add to target group if not already a member
+   - Denied identity remains ungrouped
+3. Idempotent: existing users are not recreated; already-in-group is no-op
+
+### Dry-run Behavior
+
+Read-only validation — invokes real kcadm calls to verify:
+- Realm `homelab` exists
+- Groups `audiobookshelf-users` and `audiobookshelf-admins` exist
+- Client `audiobookshelf` exists
+
+Fails immediately if any prerequisite is missing.
+
+### Security Constraints
+
+- Refuses `set -x` (xtrace) to prevent secret leakage
+- Never accepts secrets via command-line arguments
+- Never prints existing passwords or client credentials
+- Requires `KCADM` env var pointing to a kcadm binary or mock
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+| Variable | Required | Description |
+|----------|----------|-------------|
+| `KCADM` | Yes | Path to kcadm binary or mock |
+| `DRY_RUN` | No | Override dry-run mode (`true`/`false`) |
+
+## Test Coverage
+
+**Path:** `pi/tests/test_playwright_identities.sh`
+
+25 mock tests covering:
+- xtrace refusal
+- dry-run and commit modes
+- Help flag and argument validation
+- Dry-run read-only checks (realm, groups, client)
+- Dry-run failure on missing prerequisites
+- Commit mode: user creation, password rotation, group reconciliation
+- Commit mode: denied identity stays ungrouped
+- Idempotency (existing user, already-in-group)
+- Secret-free output
+- Credentials file creation, permissions, JSON validity, completeness
+
+**Note:** The previous version listed 13 tests. The count increased to 21 after
+adding fail-closed password provisioning, group reconciliation, and dry-run
+read-only prerequisite checks.
+
+Run: `bash pi/tests/test_playwright_identities.sh`
+
+## Runtime Injection
+
+### Credentials File (commit mode)
+
+After provisioning, the script writes a credentials file to:
+`$PW_E2E_CREDENTIALS_DIR/.credentials.json` (default: `~/.playwright-e2e/.credentials.json`)
+
+File permissions: `0600` (owner-only read/write).
+
+```json
+{
+  "pw-e2e-abs-user": {"username": "pw-e2e-abs-user", "password": "<generated>"},
+  "pw-e2e-abs-admin": {"username": "pw-e2e-abs-admin", "password": "<generated>"},
+  "pw-e2e-abs-denied": {"username": "pw-e2e-abs-denied", "password": "<generated>"}
+}
+```
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+The Playwright test runner reads the credentials file at startup and injects:
+- `PW_E2E_ABS_USER` — username
+- `PW_E2E_ABS_PASSWORD` — password
+
+Passwords are never committed to code or printed to stdout/stderr.
